<article class="env-lemma" id="00SM">
       
      
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00SM">Lemma <span data-tag="00SM">10.136.2</span>.</a> Let $R \to S$ be a ring map. Let $R \to R'$ be a faithfully flat ring map. Set $S' = R'\otimes _ R S$. Then $R \to S$ is syntomic if and only if $R' \to S'$ is syntomic. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Lemma <a href="/tag/00QQ" data-tag="00QQ">10.126.2</a> and Lemma <a href="/tag/00HJ" data-tag="00HJ">10.39.8</a> this holds for the property of being flat and for the property of being of finite presentation. The map $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(R') \to \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(R)$ is surjective, see Lemma <a href="/tag/00HQ" data-tag="00HQ">10.39.16</a>. Thus it suffices to show given primes $\mathfrak p' \subset R'$ lying over $\mathfrak p \subset R$ that $S \otimes _ R \kappa (\mathfrak p)$ is a local complete intersection if and only if $S' \otimes _{R'} \kappa (\mathfrak p')$ is a local complete intersection. Note that $S' \otimes _{R'} \kappa (\mathfrak p') = S \otimes _ R \kappa (\mathfrak p) \otimes _{\kappa (\mathfrak p)} \kappa (\mathfrak p')$. Thus Lemma <a href="/tag/00SJ" data-tag="00SJ">10.135.11</a> applies. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>